---
import BaseLayout from '@/components/layout/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '@/components/layout/Breadcrumbs.astro';

const updated = '2026-11-15';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="What SoloYolo collects (almost nothing), how cookies and advertising work, and the choices you control."
  path="/privacy/"
>
  <div class="container-page">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Privacy policy' }]} />

    <article class="max-w-3xl pt-8 pb-16 sm:pt-12">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-[clamp(2.1rem,1.4rem+3.4vw,3.4rem)] font-medium leading-[1.05] tracking-[-0.03em]">
        Privacy policy
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted">Last updated: <time datetime={updated}>{updated}</time></p>

      <div class="prose-ledger mt-10">
        <p>
          This policy explains what information SoloYolo ("the site", "we") handles when you use
          the site, and the choices you have. The short version: the tools themselves collect
          nothing, and you decide whether advertising cookies are used at all.
        </p>

        <h2>Information the tools collect</h2>
        <p>
          None. Every calculator runs entirely in your browser. The numbers you enter — income
          targets, expenses, hours, client details — are never sent to a server, never stored
          anywhere except in the page you have open, and disappear when you close the tab. There is
          no account and no upload.
        </p>

        <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Essential local storage.</strong> Your cookie choice is saved in your browser's
            local storage under <code>soloyolo-consent</code>. This is a single technical value
            ("all" or "essential"); it is not sent anywhere and holds no personal data.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Advertising cookies.</strong> Only if you choose <em>Accept all</em> in the
            cookie banner. When advertising is enabled, Google and its partners may set cookies to
            serve and measure ads, including personalised ads where allowed.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          If you choose <em>Essential only</em>, no advertising scripts are loaded at all — not
          just personalised ads disabled, but no ad requests made.
        </p>

        <h2>Advertising</h2>
        <p>
          The site displays ads served through <strong>Google AdSense</strong>. When advertising is
          enabled:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on your prior
            visits to this or other websites.
          </li>
          <li>
            Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads based on
            your visits to this and other sites.
          </li>
          <li>
            You can opt out of personalised advertising in
            <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ads Settings</a>
            or opt out of third-party vendor cookies at
            <a href="https://www.aboutads.info" rel="noopener noreferrer">aboutads.info</a>.
          </li>
          <li>
            For visitors in the European Economic Area and the United Kingdom, ads only load after
            you give consent, in line with the EU user consent policy.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Ads are clearly separated from content, are never disguised as tools or navigation, and
          do not influence which tools are built or how they calculate.
        </p>

        <h2>Server logs</h2>
        <p>
          The site is served statically through a hosting provider, whose infrastructure processes
          standard technical logs (for example IP addresses and request times) for security and
          abuse prevention. We do not use these logs to profile visitors, and we do not add
          analytics trackers.
        </p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct or delete personal
          data, to object to processing, or to withdraw consent. Because the tools collect no
          personal data, most requests will simply concern your cookie choice: clear your browser
          storage for this site, or email
          <a href="mailto:hello@soloyolo.example">hello@soloyolo.example</a> with "Privacy" in the
          subject line and we will help.
        </p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>
          The site is aimed at working professionals and is not directed at children under 13. We
          do not knowingly collect data from children.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          If the tools, hosting or advertising set-up changes, this page will be updated and the
          "last updated" date above will change. Material changes to advertising or cookies will be
          reflected in the cookie banner as well.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
